Implemented checked Tix-to-CUDA lowering. [`src/tensor/index.ts`](src/tensor/index.ts) exports `cudaSource`, `runTixCuda`, and `checkLowering`. The backend emits directly from the current Tix IR, preserves sequential reduction order after `inline` and `split-sum`, and preloads kernels before timing. The contract batches GPU cases against the immediate revision’s f64 reference and reuses decided verdicts.

[`tools/cuda-remote.mjs`](tools/cuda-remote.mjs) now supports opt-in source-only compile caching, isolated run directories, and locked, atomic binary publication. **No framework files changed.** The only addition to the reviewed design was a `--gpu-only` switch in [`corpus/tensor/benchmark.mjs`](corpus/tensor/benchmark.mjs).

**Verification:** `npm run build` passed. `node --test tests/tensor/*.test.mjs` passed 19 tests with 6 GPU tests skipped; `TIX_TEST_GPU=1 node --test tests/tensor/cuda-gpu.test.mjs` passed all 6. The full suite was not run.

| Workload | GB10 median (ms) | f32 interpreter wall time (s) |
|---|---:|---:|
| matmul | 0.1886 | 819.1 |
| softmax | 0.7602 | 67.5 |
| layernorm | 0.5452 | 97.8 |
| attention | 0.9680 | 501.2 |
| mlp | 1.1457 | 1,354.1 |
| conv2d | 0.3076 | 847.5 |

All six full-size outputs matched the f32 interpreter bit-for-bit on the measured inputs. The [results report](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-C--checked-tix-lowering-to-cuda-on-the-gpu-machine/reference/02-cuda-lowering-results.md) records timing ranges and sampled contract evidence. GPU times exclude startup and transfers; CPU times include shared-machine contention.

Commits: `57afcc9` initial design, `51a738b` review revisions, `214fb75` implementation, `30a13b4` verification and benchmarks. Worktree clean; nothing pushed.
